1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Welcome to the introduction to Python programming.

2
00:00:03,500 --> 00:00:07,000
In this course we will learn about variables and data types.

3
00:00:07,500 --> 00:00:12,000
A variable is a name that refers to a value stored in memory.

4
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:17,000
Python supports several data types including integers floats and strings.

5
00:00:17,500 --> 00:00:22,000
The append method adds an element to the end of a list.

6
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:27,000
A dictionary maps keys to values using curly braces and colons.

7
00:00:27,500 --> 00:00:32,000
Recursion occurs when a function calls itself during execution.

8
00:00:32,500 --> 00:00:37,000
Functions are defined using the def keyword in Python.

9
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:42,000
The return statement sends a value back to the caller of the function.

10
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:48,000
Lists are mutable sequences that support indexing and slicing operations.
